Subject: [PATCH 38/46] EXPERIMENT: gate consuming x87 pop tag correction
 (default off)

Family: consuming x87 stack pops
Members: FYL2X D9 F1, FYL2XP1 D9 F9, FPATAN D9 F3; ordinary POPSTACKDESTROY; FINCSTP D9 F7 is non-consuming and excluded.
Trigger: D9 F1, captured Heroes III states 185 and 199.
Coverage: all three transcendental siblings use shared StackPop invalidation in slow mode. Virtual stack already clears validity; ordinary destroy-pop already clears it; FINCSTP remains unchanged.
Regression: nine directed sibling/TOP0/6/7 witnesses have matching tags; two real-state FYL2X prefix replays EQUAL. OFF vs pre-fix objects: 45 architectural outputs byte-identical. Strict nine FNSTENV witnesses retain old FIP/FOP-zero discrepancy also present in accepted control. Full two-base/app acceptance NOT_ENABLED pending low32 signing and stand adjudication; no GOAL claim.
Gate: MACRUNNER_HB_X87_FIX_POP_TAG=1, default off.
Audit completed: yes (implementation family); acceptance incomplete as stated.
